KOS: add the KOS security module (security/kos)

The kernel half of KOS, against Linux 6.12.116 (see kernel/KERNEL_VERSION).
Tells apps from the core, and for every confined process: default-deny
connect/bind/listen/send unless the core wrote an exact rule, device nodes
limited to null/zero/full/random/urandom, no bpf/perf_event_open/ptrace, and
a log of every allowed and denied connection attempt.

Registers LSM_ID_KOS (114) - this number is not allocated upstream.
include/linux/lsm_count.h must count the module or the LSM framework silently
drops it for lack of static-call slots.

